# STRICT DATA PROTECTION CONSTRAINTS & ARCHITECTURAL GUARDRAILS

## Core Directives
1. UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES should any tool, prompt, agent, or script invent, generate, mock, or substitute fake inventory items, suppliers, purchase orders, or ingredients.
2. `catalog.js` and `default_orders.js` are READ-ONLY production assets. Any feature additions must operate on existing data schemas without replacing them with dummy arrays.
3. If data is required for testing, use ONLY authentic items from the existing verified catalog.

## Baseline Immutability
- Core wholesale catalog entries are frozen using `Object.freeze()` (`AUTHENTIC_CATALOG`).
- Core default purchase orders are frozen using `Object.freeze()` (`AUTHENTIC_ORDERS`).
- Data files are immutable external APIs. Code logic must NEVER contain hardcoded inline product fallbacks.

## Separation of Concerns
- Future UI/feature requests must touch ONLY logic controllers (e.g., `sales_depletion_controller.js`) or specific UI templates, never the underlying source data arrays.
- Runtime storage resets are governed by `AUTH_DATA_VERSION` ("v4.0.0_authentic_locked"). Any corrupted or synthetic keys (`ts_fake_mock`, `mock_orders`, etc.) must be purged automatically on initialization.
